Z||000006||Cheever2||08-06-2001||07:29 PM||||U mean the sun roof sun shade?  My 88 GT came with it, but it sux.  Came with Velcro buttons to mount it with - yeah, right.  And it's so friggin frail and flimsy.  Just touching it leaves an imprint.  I just keep it in the bag on a shelf in the garage.<P>Somebody make one that actually fits, and mounts <I>securely</I>, okay?  Thanks.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||08-06-2001||08:35 PM||||I thought about using a shade. either OE or repro... Too much of a pain to fool with... One more thing to find space to store. <P>I didn't like that they totally block the roof. I went with 2 12x16 plastic cling shades like you use on a side window to preotect a kid seat. Makes a major diferance but doesn't totally block the glass. You can still see thru them.<P>The shade was suposed to come with most of the later cars that have the sunroof. (I didn't think 84-85 had them at all.) I'm the third owner of my car, so I didn't get one... Other than as a show item, I'd never use one.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||JohnF||08-07-2001||08:06 AM||||I wouldn't be without!  <P>I use sun shade almost continuously during the summer here in the Lone Star State.  Besides my head staying cooler (and entire interior staying cooler) it tends to help block harmful sun rays to interior.  Especially this interior which warps so badly.<P>During shows, the shade is stored in the bag and placed under the roof in the front trunk (which holds both nicely) or is used toi cover the bottom portion of the rear trunk with the word "Fiero" prominent.<P>I added more "velcro" than the factory corner circles to ensure that the shade stayed in the up position for car venting.||||reg||6
